Third-party notes
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Script Hook V
  https://www.dev-c.com/gtav/scripthookv
  (C) Alexander Blade. Closed-source freeware.

  NOT included, NOT redistributed, NOT linked at build time. The plugin
  resolves ScriptHookV.dll's exported functions by name at run time
  (src/shv.cpp). No file here is copied or derived from Script Hook V
  or its SDK; test/mock_shv.cpp is an independent stand-in that exports
  the same symbol names for off-device testing.

GTA V NativeDB
  https://github.com/alloc8or/gta5-nativedb-data
  Community reference. The native names, identifiers and parameter
  lists in src/natives.h were checked against natives.json and
  natives_gen9.json. No file from that repository is included.

CodeWalker (GTAKeys.cs)
  https://github.com/dexyfex/CodeWalker (MIT, (c) 2015 Neodymium)
  The 375 SHA-1 fingerprints shipped in ../common/keys_v.cpp come
  from CodeWalker's GTAKeys.cs. That file self-attests "contains
  only SHA1 hashes of all interesting values. There is NO key." We
  reproduce those hex digests verbatim as string literals so the
  companion can locate GTA V's AES key, 101 NG keys, 272 NG decrypt
  tables, and the lookup table inside each user's own GTA5.exe at
  install time. No key / table bytes are included; only the hashes
  that locate them.

Unlike asi/ (GTA IV), nothing in this directory is derived from
GTAIV.EFLC.FusionFix or Zolika1351/iv-sdk.
